=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the cache-then-network data port, also Microsoft.UI-free),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view).
  Namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews. The TeslaChargingSessionsMap surface already exists (built by the
  predecessor component prompt p2-windows/feature-views/W-0120-TeslaChargingSessionsMap, commit 840b28474, in the
  base integration branch); this page-parity unit verifies it against the 7 manifest items, fixes the two real
  defects that blocked an honest green gate (below), adds the markerLabel regression test, runs the windows triad,
  and records the ledger row. The web component is the (unrouted) <MapContainer>/<MarkerCluster> map that the
  charging-history page passes its useTeslaChargingSessions() `sessions` into — no standalone nav item.
- Data source (web page's useTeslaChargingSessions() · GET /tesla/charging/sessions/): the Microsoft.UI-free
  ITeslaChargingSessionsMapSource / repository-backed TeslaChargingSessionsMapSource runs one cache-then-network
  read of the generated operation get_api_v1_tesla_charging_sessions through the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine
  (cacheKey tesla:charging:sessions:map), parsing each emission into TeslaChargingSessionsMapData (the
  { sessions:[…] } envelope OR a bare array, with numeric-string coercion). No HTTP touches the view.
- Projection (web useMemo(center) + useMemo(clusterPoints)): TeslaChargingSessionsMapProjection.Project is the 1:1
  port — center = mean of every session's (lat ?? 0, lng ?? 0) falling back to the SF view { 37.77, -122.42 } at
  zoom 5; a marker is emitted for every session with a FINITE lat/lng (web typeof===number && !isNaN); the popup
  mirrors the web popupHtml (fmtNumber(convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh'),1)+' kWh', formatCurrency(cost,2), the
  uppercased charger type) and the Narrator label resolves tesla_sessions.markerLabel. Every label flows through
  ILocalizer; the view binds the projected viewport + markers and stays a thin renderer.
- Units (P1/S5): total_energy_added_wh is SI watt-hours on the wire; the popup restates it via the shared
  UnitConverters.EnergyFromSi(wh, EnergyUnit.Kwh) + ScalarFormatters.FormatNumber at projection time — the "kWh"
  unit is intrinsic to the web popup string. Nothing non-SI is stored or computed.
- Defect 1 fixed (pre-existing build blocker, in this prompt's allowed "NavigationView registration" file):
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs had a malformed page-factory block — the "AutomationList"
  registration lambda was never closed (missing `return page; });`), so the sibling "Automations" registration and
  every later statement were swallowed into its body. That unbalanced the constructor braces (CS1026/CS1002/CS1513
  at line 146) and cascaded into a WMC9999 XAML-compiler crash on every XAML file (130×WMC0001 + 30×WMC0110), i.e.
  the whole solution was red and the page could not be built/verified at all. Repaired by closing the AutomationList
  lambda (the un-nested Automations/AutomationBuilder/BatteryDegradation/ProjectedRange registrations are unchanged).
- Defect 2 fixed (real runtime i18n parity bug in the surface, allowed feature dir):
  TeslaChargingSessionsMapRegistration.MarkerLabel composed the marker's accessible label with
  GetString("tesla_sessions.markerLabel", "{{name}} charging session").Replace("{{name}}", name). But the shared
  i18n generator (apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts, placeholderFor() case 'windows' → "{idx}") renders the
  web i18next "{{name}}" token as the positional string.Format placeholder "{0}" in the .resw catalog (the
  canonical Windows form — 417 "{0}"-style values vs 4 "{{}}" in en/Resources.resw). With the real catalog value
  "{0} charging session", the literal Replace("{{name}}",…) was a no-op, so every marker's Narrator label would
  have surfaced as the raw "{0} charging session" (a11y parity break). Fixed to read the "{0}" fallback and compose
  with string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, template, name) — mirroring the web t('…', { name }) call and the
  app-wide convention (e.g. ProjectedRange range.whatIfConditions). Added a regression test
  (Marker_label_interpolates_the_generated_catalog_token) that feeds the real "{0} charging session" catalog
  value through a CatalogLocalizer and asserts "Fremont SC charging session" / "Unknown charging session", so a
  revert to the literal-replace form fails the build.
- Catalog: the 3 web i18n keys (tesla_sessions.mapLabel / markerLabel / unknown) plus the empty-overlay key
  (tesla_sessions.noMapData) already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (mapLabel "Charging
  sessions map", markerLabel "{0} charging session", unknown "Unknown"). No catalog rows added; every visible
  literal resolves through ILocalizer with the web key names.

